      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum metformin dose. The labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nCould this be a typo? Some possibilities:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the max for immediate-release.\n- **500 mg three times daily**, which is 1,500 mg/day.\n- **1000 mg twice daily**, which is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **1700 mg total daily**, split into a different schedule.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you really do intend 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly and give me a note for the order, and I'll enter it as written."
      }
     ],
